quotes.quote:
ProtoJSON HTTP PATCH body:

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "displayName": "Summer"
  },
  "updateMask": "displayName"
}
```

Expected stored resource, derived from the contract:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Summer",
  "description": "Approved",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}
```

The mask is a ProtoJSON string containing a resource-relative path. `name` identifies the campaign; it is not selected for mutation.

Starting independently from the original before state:

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "description": ""
  },
  "updateMask": "description"
}
```

Expected stored resource:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Spring",
  "description": "",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}
```

If serialization omits the empty `description`, this contract still resets it: a selected scalar absent from the normalized message receives its default. The mask must survive serialization.
